From: NixOS Android devices contributors <nixos-android-devices@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 05:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: wire Asphalt DisplayPort and track DP orientation

Local adaptation against Linux v7.3-rc4 and this board's patch queue.
The preserved stock live DT selects GLINK altmode port 0 and i2c5 FSA4480
at 0x43 for DP AUX. Connect those endpoints and enable the existing DP0
controller. Both USB ports still share DWC3 without assigning its role
switch to only one connector. Do not attach the secondary FSA4480 at
0x42, which is not the AUX switch selected by the stock DP controller.

Retain hardware COM port selection for USB, but accept orientation updates
for DP's lane power and PHY_MODE programming. Rejecting these notifications
also aborts the typec switch chain before the AUX mux can be configured.

Stock driver reference (DP AUX CC1/CC2 settings, local implementation):
https://github.com/lolipuru/kernel_lenovo_sm8475/blob/9b7833ce5db1a9914dc5e5e06d1a0cccfdd5c73b/drivers/soc/qcom/fsa4480-i2c.c
Upstream graph reference:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3-rc4/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450-hdk.dts
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-asphalt.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-asphalt.dts
index bd11263cf..78a862a72 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-asphalt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-lenovo-asphalt.dts
@@ -87,6 +87,26 @@ connector@0 {
 			reg = <0>;
 			power-role = "dual";
 			data-role = "dual";
+
+			/* Stock DP altmode client 0 uses the primary FSA4480. */
+			ports {
+				#address-cells = <1>;
+				#size-cells = <0>;
+
+				port@1 {
+					reg = <1>;
+					pmic_glink_dp_ss: endpoint {
+						remote-endpoint = <&usb_1_qmpphy_out>;
+					};
+				};
+
+				port@2 {
+					reg = <2>;
+					pmic_glink_dp_sbu: endpoint {
+						remote-endpoint = <&fsa4480_sbu>;
+					};
+				};
+			};
 		};
 
 		connector@1 {
@@ -501,6 +521,20 @@ backlight: backlight@11 {
 &i2c5 {
 	status = "okay";
 
+	/* Powered by the board; downstream does not control a supply here. */
+	typec-mux@43 {
+		compatible = "fcs,fsa4480";
+		reg = <0x43>;
+		mode-switch;
+		orientation-switch;
+
+		port {
+			fsa4480_sbu: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&pmic_glink_dp_sbu>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
 	eusb2_repeater: phy@4f {
 		compatible = "nxp,eusb2-repeater";
 		reg = <0x4f>;
@@ -1132,3 +1166,16 @@ camera_mclk2: camera-mclk2-state {
   bias-disable;
  };
 };
+
+/* DisplayPort is wired to the primary Type-C connector (GLINK port 0). */
+&mdss_dp0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdss_dp0_out {
+	data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
+};
+
+&usb_1_qmpphy_out {
+	remote-endpoint = <&pmic_glink_dp_ss>;
+};
diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 91db9130c..119b07ab5 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4785,9 +4785,11 @@ static int qmp_combo_typec_switch_set(struct typec_switch_dev *sw,
 	struct qmp_combo *qmp = typec_switch_get_drvdata(sw);
 	const struct qmp_phy_cfg *cfg = qmp->cfg;
 
-	if (qmp->hardware_port_select)
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-
+	/*
+	 * Even with hardware COM port selection, DP lane power and PHY_MODE
+	 * still need the connector orientation. Keep the ordinary state update;
+	 * qmp_combo_com_init() continues to select the hardware input.
+	 */
 	if (orientation == qmp->orientation || orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE)
 		return 0;
 
